 "text": "Hi, how are you doing right now? Roughly half of the people get under a good tarp and pull it tight. The others stand by a light rain window and pass the tarp with ropes. Then get everyone inside as quickly as you can. If you can see lightning or hear thunder, count ten seconds and stop. If it' dry enough, open a small window for air. Sure, nod again and I' light them. Put the tent up first so it's done and the tent is dry ground you can pack it. Then pack the tent as quickly as possible. Set up the tent again and stay dry. There are usually cafes and hotels near the trailhead. Get everyone inside and put a tarp down. Then pack the tent and get going. Try to reach a cabin tonight if you can.",
